;; Worked intent example — scaffolded by `sl init`.
;;
;; Intents give page elements NAMES so features can say Login.username
;; instead of repeating raw locators. An unquoted Capitalized.dotted name
;; (Intent.element) is a glossary reference, resolved at planning time — an
;; unknown name is a plan error with a did-you-mean. (Curly braces mean
;; something else: {name} is a value from the scenario data plane, captured
;; earlier; '…' in single quotes is literal content.)
;;
;; The intent loader reads every *.edn file in this directory; this file's
;; .example suffix keeps it INVISIBLE to the loader. Rename it to login.edn
;; (and match the locators to your app) to activate.
;;
;; This intent describes the login page the starter feature
;; (features/login.feature) drives — once active, its steps can become e.g.:
;;   And :user/alice fills Login.username with 'alice'
{:intent "Login"
 :elements {:username {:bindings {:web {:id "username"}}}
            :password {:bindings {:web {:id "password"}}}
            :submit   {:bindings {:web {:css "button[type=\"submit\"]"}}}}}
